.TH SONGBIRD-GAMING 1 "January 2025" "songbird-orchestrator 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
songbird-gaming \- Gaming network bridge commands for legacy game protocol detection and bridging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B songbird gaming
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,COMMAND\/\fR [\fI\,ARGS\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The gaming subcommand provides network bridging capabilities for legacy games from the 1990s and 2000s. It can detect gaming protocols and create bridges to make LAN-only games playable over the internet.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan the local network for active gaming sessions
.TP
.B bridge
Create a network bridge for detected gaming sessions
.TP
.B list
List all detected gaming sessions and their status
.TP
.B stop
Stop active gaming bridges
.TP
.B status
Show status of gaming bridge services

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-\-game " " \fI\,GAME\/\fR
Specify game type (starcraft, aoe2, cnc, etc.)
.TP
.BR \-\-protocol " " \fI\,PROTOCOL\/\fR
Force specific protocol detection (ipx, directplay, netbios, udp, tcp)
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fI\,PORT\/\fR
Specify port for bridge listening
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fI\,SECONDS\/\fR
Timeout for scanning operations (default: 10)

.SH SUPPORTED GAMES
.TP
.B StarCraft (1998)
Protocol: IPX, Typical ports: 6112-6119
.TP
.B Age of Empires II (1999) 
Protocol: DirectPlay, Typical ports: 2300-2400, 47624
.TP
.B Command & Conquer (1995)
Protocol: IPX, Typical ports: 1140, 8086
.TP
.B Age of Empires (1997)
Protocol: DirectPlay, Typical ports: 2300-2400
.TP
.B Warcraft II (1995)
Protocol: IPX, Typical ports: 213, 6112-6119

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B songbird gaming scan
Scan for any active gaming sessions on the local network
.TP
.B songbird gaming scan --game starcraft
Scan specifically for StarCraft gaming sessions
.TP
.B songbird gaming bridge --game starcraft --port 6112
Create a bridge for StarCraft on port 6112
.TP
.B songbird gaming list
List all currently detected gaming sessions
.TP
.B songbird gaming status
Show status of all active gaming bridges
.TP
.B songbird gaming stop
Stop all active gaming bridges

.SH PROTOCOL DETECTION
Songbird uses real packet capture to detect gaming protocols:
.TP
.B IPX Detection
Looks for IPX packet headers and game-specific signatures
.TP
.B DirectPlay Detection  
Identifies DirectPlay enumeration and connection packets
.TP
.B NetBIOS Detection
Detects NetBIOS name resolution and session packets
.TP
.B UDP/TCP Detection
Generic UDP/TCP gaming traffic pattern analysis

.SH BRIDGE OPERATION
When a bridge is created, Songbird:
.IP 1. 4
Captures packets from the detected gaming session
.IP 2. 4
Translates legacy protocols to modern internet-routable formats
.IP 3. 4
Provides NAT traversal and connection brokering
.IP 4. 4
Maintains session state and handles reconnections

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/songbird/gaming.toml
Gaming-specific configuration
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/songbird/gaming/
Gaming session data and logs

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SONGBIRD_GAMING_INTERFACE
Network interface for packet capture (default: auto-detect)
.TP
.B SONGBIRD_GAMING_TIMEOUT
Default timeout for gaming operations in seconds

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
No gaming sessions detected
.TP
.B 2
Bridge creation failed
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied (packet capture requires elevated privileges)

.SH NOTES
Gaming protocol detection requires elevated privileges for packet capture. Run with sudo/administrator privileges or configure appropriate capabilities.

Some legacy games may require additional configuration or compatibility settings. Refer to the game-specific documentation.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR songbird (1),
.BR songbird-orchestrator (1),
.BR pcap (3)

